  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P><STRONG>Bizzare column on The Sun newspaper:</STRONG></P>
<P><FONT size=2><SPAN class=black24><STRONG><FONT face=Verdana>Madge twangs her G-string</FONT></STRONG></SPAN> </FONT></P>
<P><SPAN class=postbody><STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> is re-inventing herself again - this time as <STRONG>the Queen of Rock</STRONG>.</SPAN></P>
<P><SPAN class=postbody>The undisputed pop goddess has nearly finished her next album and it will have a heave guitar sound. </SPAN></P>
<P><SPAN class=postbody>I've got my hands on a secret blueprint for the new material which is out at the end of the year. <BR>I can reveal the poppy, dance feel of the last release American Life has gone in favour of an ore edgy theme. <BR>Madonna will even play most of the big guitar riffs herself. Her inspiration has come from the rise of British guitar rock bands.&nbsp;A source close to Madge told me "Living in Britain she has become a real fan of <STRONG>Franz Ferdinand</STRONG> and love the kitshy sound of <STRONG>The Darkness</STRONG>. </SPAN></P>
<P><SPAN class=postbody>"She is moving more in that direction - real sounds, like a real band. </SPAN></P>
<P><SPAN class=postbody></SPAN><SPAN class=postbody>"She is close to finishing the new album and there is a real hard rock feel to it. </SPAN></P>
<P><SPAN class=postbody>"Madonna always keeps in touch with what is popular in the charts and has been really into the guitar-based rock bands of 2004. <STRONG>The new album is taking shape as one of her best ever." <BR><BR></STRONG>She has enlisted help from several big name producers for the project. <STRONG>Swedish duo Bloodshy &amp; Avant</STRONG>, who produced Toxic for Britney Spears have asked to write a song. <BR>Christian "Bloodshy" Karlsson and Pontus "Avant " Winnberg won a Grammy for Toxic just this week. Winnberg revealed Madonna called them in person to make sure they took the job - but their contribution will be less rocky than the other tracks. He said "We're going to give Madonnas sound a real disco feel". </SPAN></P>
<P><SPAN class=postbody>Madge is also working with French electro whizz <STRONG>Mirwais and Stuart Price</STRONG> - the main producer. The album will include a cover of <STRONG>John Lennon's Imagine</STRONG>, which she showcased during last year's tour. </SPAN></P>
<P><SPAN class=postbody><STRONG>Monte Pittman, her official guitarist and teacher, has co-written a rock song called "I Love New York" ** and she will record the riffs</STRONG>. </SPAN></P>
<P><SPAN class=postbody><EM>Victoria Newton</EM></SPAN></P>
<P><SPAN class=postbody><EM><STRONG>** a <A href="http://www.drownedmadonna.com/">Drownedmadonna</A> Exclusive</STRONG></EM></SPAN></P>
</font></div>
	</td>
  </tr>
