  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P><STRONG>New York</STRONG> fashion shows are just over.&nbsp; <STRONG>London</STRONG> fashion shows are just started. <STRONG>Milan</STRONG> fashion shows are going to start in a week. In the meantime, most of the&nbsp;women's wear for the next winter has been already bought from (professional) buyers.&nbsp;So&nbsp;we can draw&nbsp;conclusions and see which are the fashion houses that mostly satisfy business demands.&nbsp;Which means that we can understand&nbsp;the fashion houses that are&nbsp;meeting with the&nbsp;biggest success, the fashion houses that will probably meet&nbsp;with the biggest&nbsp;public favour.&nbsp;Before seeing the collections&nbsp;at the fashion shows, professional buyers already&nbsp;made the most of their choices, buying the so-called "pre-collections".</P>
<P><STRONG>Versace is back in vogue and it's supposed to have a 20%&nbsp;sales increase due to the new ad campaign featuring Madonna.</STRONG></P>
</font></div>
