 <table width="100%" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" cellpadding="5">
  <tr>
    <td background="images/bg.gif"><font class=""><a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=44">Upcoming Projects</a></font><br><font class="testo_notizia" color="#000000"><b>[<a href="modules.php?name=&amp;file=categories&amp;op=newindex&amp;catid=10"><font class="esclusiva">BREAKING NEWS</font></a>] Some More About The ReInvention DVD.</b></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td  background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P><STRONG><EM>Optimus</EM></STRONG>, a good insider is providing the <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>'s community with the<STRONG> latest</STRONG> about the<STRONG> DVD/Documentary project</STRONG>.</P>
<P>We decided to publish his info (which matches <STRONG>our inside exclusives published back in Autumn 2004</STRONG>) because he is <STRONG><U>absolutely realible</U></STRONG>.</P>
<P><EM><STRONG>"</STRONG>There is no scheduled release date at the moment but <STRONG>the DVD will be released</STRONG>. In fact the DVD is near completed last I heard. I repeat, the RIT will be released.<BR><BR>No one at Warner including Liz Rosenburg will give a straight answer because there is no confirmed date yet. Until a solid 100% release date is confirmed they will deflect all inquiries with generic vague statements.<BR><BR><STRONG>The reason for the delay is that they want to focus on the documentary</STRONG>. They want to delay the release of the RIT so as to draw more people to the doc. <STRONG>The doc is Madonna's passion and focus at the moment</STRONG>.<BR><BR>As it stands it seems <STRONG>the concert will be released on either sometime after the release of the documentary or at the same time that the documentary itself is released on DVD in order to maximize exposure to both.</STRONG></EM></P>
<P><STRONG></STRONG><EM>It was at one point planned for Spring 2005 but then they started playing with the idea of releasing it after the documentary. There is a chance they could stick with their original release of Spring 2005 but at this point it is unlikely.<STRONG> This is why there is so much confusion among retailers because they did receive advance release info only to have it retracted and left obscure.<BR></STRONG></EM><BR><EM>Last bit I can throw in is that <STRONG>there might be a single released at the same time as the documentary</STRONG>. Right now the idea of releasing <STRONG>Imagine</STRONG> is being toyed with. <STRONG>Part of the reason Madonna sang it at Tsunami Aid was as a test</STRONG>.<BR><BR>Just remember that with Madonna everything is done for a reason. She's a very smart business woman.<STRONG>"</STRONG></EM></P>
<P><EM>A <STRONG>special </STRONG>thanks to <STRONG>Optimus</STRONG></EM></P>
<P><STRONG>Previous related News:</STRONG></P>
<P><STRONG><IMG src="/images/rombo.jpg" border=0>&nbsp;[<A href="modules.php?name=News&amp;file=categories&amp;op=newindex&amp;catid=2"><FONT class=esclusiva color=#000000>EXCLUSIVE</FONT></A>]<A href="http://www.drownedmadonna.com/modules.php?name=News&amp;file=article&amp;sid=5123"> Madonna's plans for the Future</A>, <EM>article from November 2004.</EM></STRONG></P>
</font></div>
	</td>
